mastery.question_text:
When people of the same weight walk in snow, the depth $D$ cm of a footprint varies inversely with the area $A$ cm$^{2}$ of the shoe sole, as shown. Use the graph to find the model, then find the sole area of a person whose footprint is $2.5$ cm deep.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=8.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-90,xmax=2080,ymin=-1,ymax=12.5,xtick={0,300,...,1800},ytick={0,1,...,12},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$A$},ylabel={$D$},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=313:2050,samples=140] {3600/x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
